1
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:03,840
Oh, hey, Joey.

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,900
- Hey. - Listen, I need to ask you something.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,300
You know how my stepdad's in prison?

4
00:00:11,194 --> 00:00:13,094
- Yeah. - Yeah.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,260
He was supposed to get a weekend furlough so he could go to the wedding.

6
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,900
But he just called and....

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:23,400
Well, apparently stabbing lceman in the exercise yard couldn't wait till Monday.

8
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,380
- So he can't come? - No.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,540
And so there's no one to walk me down the aisle. And....

10
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,400
Well, I would just really love it if you would do it.

11
00:00:34,989 --> 00:00:36,419
- Seriously? - Yeah.

12
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:39,020
You've, you know, sort of been like a dad to me.

13
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:44,500
I mean, you've always, you know, looked out for me and shared your wisdom.

14
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,360
I am pretty "wisdomous."

15
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,680
So, what do you say?

16
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,740
Are you kidding? Phoebe, I would be honored.

17
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:59,160
Oh, thank you.

18
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,150
I hope....

19
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,920
I hope you know how much you mean to me.

20
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,000
Listen, I hope....

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,760
I hope that you know....

22
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:16,775
I don't want you to see your father cry. Go to your room!

23
00:01:18,981 --> 00:01:21,161
《老友记》第十季第十二集 菲比的婚礼

24
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:11,000
Oh, no, no, no. Let your dad get this.

25
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,360
It's my wedding planner. She's driving me crazy!

26
00:02:20,243 --> 00:02:24,123
Hello? Okay, stop screaming!

27
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,760
Okay, so halibut.

28
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:30,560
All right, so salmon. Either way. I don't--

29
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,620
It doesn't matter to me. Well, it matters to me!

30
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,140
Well, I don't care. So you pick.

31
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,920
Did you just hang up on me?

32
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,240
All right, look, I need you at the rehearsal dinner tonight at 1800 hours.

33
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,300
Okay. What time is that?

34
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,580
You don't know military time?

35
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,720
military time:24小时制

36
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,500
I must have been in missile training the day they taught that.

37
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,820
Just subtract 12.

38
00:02:56,900 --> 00:03:00,680
Okay, so 1800 minus 12 is 1788.

39
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,340
- Six o'clock! - Okay.

40
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,940
Hold on. Yeah? Geller here.

41
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:10,990
No, I said it has to be there by 4:00. Goodbye.

42
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,600
God. How hard is it to make an ice sculpture?

43
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,940
Wait. Ice sculpture? That sounds really fancy.

44
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,980
I told you, I just want a simple wedding.

45
00:03:18,117 --> 00:03:21,280
Please, honey, leave the details to me.

46
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,840
Now, I wanna make this day as special for you as I can.

47
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,660
I was thinking the harpist should wear white.

48
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,460
Harpist? My friend Marjorie is playing the steel drums.

49
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,700
Oh, she backed out. She did? Why?

50
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,140
I made her.

51
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,280
Steel drums don't really say "elegant wedding."

52
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:40,580
Nor does Marjorie's overwhelming scent. Hey!

53
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,360
She will shower when Tibet is free.

54
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:55,780
- Hey. You look great. - You too.

55
00:03:56,220 --> 00:04:00,700
I'm glad we're having a rehearsal dinner. I rarely practice my meals before I eat.

56
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,700
What did we say was your one gift to us?

57
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:08,360
No stupid jokes, but I thought that was for the actual wedding.

58
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,260
Rehearse it.

59
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,270
Hi.

60
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,460
Thanks for coming, you guys. Oh, yeah--

61
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,540
I was.... I was going for a handshake.

62
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,580
That why your hand's against my crotch?

63
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,880
- That is why. - Yeah.

64
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,900
So, Rach, where's Emma?

65
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:27,760
Monica made me send her to my mom's.

66
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,280
Apparently, babies and weddings don't mix.

67
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,360
Are you still crying about your damn baby?

68
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:38,980
Pheebs, you got to keep the line moving. Remember, 20 seconds per person.

69
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,840
You see these clowns all the time.

70
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:47,320
Hey, you're Mike's parents, right? Yes, we are.

71
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,280
Our little ones are growing up fast, aren't they?

72
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:56,820
- How's that? - You know on one hand, you're happy for them. On the other, it's hard to let go.

73
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,860
Who in God's name are you?

74
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:05,060
I'm not that fond of you either, buddy. I'm just trying to be nice for the kids.

75
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:12,420
You know what I realized? We have no idea what we're doing in the wedding tomorrow.

76
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:15,840
Yeah, I thought we'd be groomsmen. They would have asked us by now.

77
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,860
When did they ask you to be a bridesmaid?

78
00:05:18,793 --> 00:05:21,860
November. I wanna say it's not looking good.

79
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,420
- Hey, Pheebs? - Sorry?

80
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,660
You haven't told these guys what they're doing in the wedding yet.

81
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:31,240
Well, they're not in the wedding.

82
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,020
What?

83
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:40,540
Well this is really awkward.

84
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,480
Oh, and I can leave.

85
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:50,100
I'm sorry, you guys. But Mike's got his brother and his friends from school.

86
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,120
So, you know, you were....

87
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:55,840
If it helps, you were next in line. You just missed the cut.

88
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:57,900
Oh, man.

89
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,720
This is like figure skating team all over again.

90
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:04,440
figure skating/synchronized swimming/balance beam:均为女子运动项目

91
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,560
I mean, synchronized swimming.

92
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,000
I mean-- I mean, the balance beam.

93
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:11,400
- Help me. - Football.

94
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,720
Thank you.

95
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,940
Oh, Pheebs, spit that out. That has pork in it.

96
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:20,000
I thought the pot stickers were supposed to be vegetarian?

97
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,680
Yeah, I changed them. I sent you a fax about it.

98
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,760
I don't have a fax machine.

99
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,540
Well, then there are gonna be a few surprises.

100
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:36,000
I can't believe we're gonna be the only people that aren't in this wedding.

101
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,940
I know. I hate being left out of things. And it's a wedding.

102
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:41,380
It'll be weird if I'm not in it.

103
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,900
- Hey, guys, how's it going? - Fine.

104
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:50,460
We're sitting here, alone, doing nothing. It's our rehearsal for tomorrow.

105
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,640
Look, about tomorrow, I've got a question for you.

106
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,740
I found out one of my groomsmen had an emergency and can't make it.

107
00:06:57,980 --> 00:06:59,620
What happened? Who cares? And...?

108
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,040
And I was wondering if one of you guys--

109
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,440
- I'll do it! -No... Me!

110
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:09,580
You both wanna do it? There's only room for one.

111
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:12,580
Pick me. I look great in a tux, and I won't steal focus.

112
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:16,080
No, Mike. No, no, you wanna pick me. I mean.... Watch.

113
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:25,660
You know, I really don't feel very comfortable making this decision.

114
00:07:25,970 --> 00:07:28,140
You know, Phoebe knows you better. I'm gonna let her choose.

115
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:34,460
Well, if Phoebe's choosing, then say hello to Mike's next groomsman.

116
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:40,160
Oh, I will. But I will need a mirror as he is me.

117
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,320
Please. You're going down. You are going "downer."

118
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,700
They say that on the figure skating team?

119
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,600
I wouldn't know. I didn't make it.

120
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,960
You know I'm filling in for Phoebe's stepdad tomorrow, right?

121
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,800
Yeah. Yeah. Hey, thanks for doing that. Oh, hey, my pleasure.

122
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,320
So, what are your intentions with my Phoebe?

123
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,100
- I intend to marry her. - Oh, a wiseacre.

124
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:12,820
I understand you plan to support your wife by playing the piano?

125
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,640
Isn't that kind of unstable?

126
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,200
- No more so than acting. - Strike two.

127
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:24,180
You're right. She probably will support me.

128
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,820
Hey, unless we move in with you, Dad.

129
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,700
Strike three.

130
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,840
You only get one more, Mike.

131
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,720
So? What did you decide?

132
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,820
I decided to pee.

133
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,920
He didn't tell you?

134
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,820
You have to choose one of us to be in your wedding.

135
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:47,360
One of the groomsmen fell out. Oh, no, no.

136
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:50,820
I can't choose between you two. I love you both so much.

137
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:53,640
Just not enough to put us in the original wedding party.

138
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,220
But I don't wanna choose. It's....

139
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,440
Okay, wait. Rach?

140
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:03,160
Listen, I have a very special bridesmaid task for you to do.

141
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,080
Goody! What is it?

142
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:11,320
Well, there's a spot open for only one groomsman and you have to choose between Ross and Chandler. So good luck with that.

143
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:14,540
What? What, what, what? No, I don't wanna do that.

144
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,700
All right. I guess I have to find a new bridesmaid.

145
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,600
I'll do it!

146
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,960
Okay, it's 2100 hours.

147
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,740
Time for your toast. Do I have time to go to the bathroom?

148
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:27,360
You had a bathroom break at 2030. Pee on your own time, Mike.

149
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:33,600
In regards to the toasts, okay, you wanna keep them short.

150
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,700
Nothing kills a rehearsal dinner like long speeches. Okay.

151
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,840
You just get in, do your thing, and get out.

152
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,460
Is that what you say to Chandler?

153
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:45,340
It's 2101, and I am not amused.

154
00:09:47,063 --> 00:09:48,123
Okay.

155
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:51,660
The bride and groom have a few words they'd like to say.

156
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,600
Okay. Hello, everyone.

157
00:09:56,940 --> 00:10:01,000
And thank you all for being here tonight. So tomorrow's the big event.

158
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:05,120
Some of you might not know, but Mike and I didn't get off to the best start.

159
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:12,740
Yeah. My friend Joey and l decided to fix each other up with friends. So l--

160
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:16,880
Oh, okay. I....

161
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:24,260
I gave it a lot of thought, and I fixed him up with my friend Mary Ellen who couldn't be here tonight, because.... It's not--

162
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:27,540
It's not important. Well, she's in rehab.

163
00:10:29,606 --> 00:10:39,120
Anyway. So Joey said that he was fixing me up with his friend Mike only he didn't have a friend Mike, so he just brought my Mike. And-- And--

164
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:43,140
But despite, you know-- It got good.

165
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:49,320
Ok, I wanna take a moment to mention my mother, who couldn't be here.

166
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,510
Oh, God.

167
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,230
And.... And moment's over.

168
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:56,040
So okay.... Oh, no, forget that.

169
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:58,460
I can forget that. Oh, this is funny.

170
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,580
Oh, but you need to know that to get that.

171
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,440
So.... Oh, well, okay.

172
00:11:05,454 --> 00:11:07,884
I.... Okay.

173
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,280
Okay, Monica, I can't do it like this!

174
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:16,060
This is my wedding, okay? I don't want this--

175
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,500
Or this-- Or this--

176
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:24,180
Okay? I just wanted a simple wedding where my fiance can go to the bathroom any time he wants!

177
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,080
- You know what? You're done. - What?

178
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,080
You're fired!

179
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,120
Cheers.

180
00:11:45,377 --> 00:11:47,077
- Hey. - Happy wedding day.

181
00:11:47,163 --> 00:11:48,843
Happy my wedding day to you.

182
00:11:50,132 --> 00:11:53,142
Joey, listen, this is gonna be bridesmaid central, all right?

183
00:11:53,204 --> 00:11:55,427
We're gonna have hair and makeup in the bathroom.

184
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,060
I had to move a couple things in the fridge to make room for the corsages.

185
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,450
因为瑞秋说要把corsage放到冰箱里  乔伊以为可以吃

186
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:02,560
Man! I wouldn't have had breakfast if I knew there was gonna be corsages.

187
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,940
Hi.

188
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:10,540
About last night....

189
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,980
I know you're under a lot of stress, and....

190
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,760
Well, even though the things you said

191
00:12:17,922 --> 00:12:19,722
...as someone who's never been fired before--

192
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,420
My point is....

193
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,620
Well, I'm willing to take my job back.

194
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,420
Oh, well, that's okay.

195
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:33,000
I think you and I will do much better if you're just here as a bridesmaid.

196
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:36,320
Is that so?

197
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,360
Okay.

198
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:41,060
If that's really what you want, then here.

199
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:44,700
I give you the headset. I don't really wanna give you the headset.

200
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:50,140
I guess if you're taking over, then you should probably return these messages.

201
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,040
Wow. This is a lot.

202
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:59,260
But I'm sure you can handle this. I have won awards for my organizational skills. But I'm sure you'll do fine.

203
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,180
You've won awards? I printed them out on my computer.

204
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,160
- Hey. - Hi.

205
00:13:06,335 --> 00:13:08,340
Where's Rach? She's in her room. Why?

206
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,000
I have to talk to her about this groomsman situation.

207
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:14,740
Ok, I'm not gonna watch Chandler up there while I'm in the seats like some chump.

208
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,540
My God, you're breathtaking.

209
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:26,720
What do you want?

210
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:31,340
You haven't by any chance chosen a groomsman yet, have you?

211
00:13:31,758 --> 00:13:34,700
Ross, please don't make this harder than it already is.

212
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:37,140
I'm not. I'm making it easier. Pick me.

213
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:42,160
Chandler said it's important to him too. Listen. Listen.

214
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:45,860
Whoever you pick is gonna walk down the aisle with you.

215
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:52,820
Now, I promise I won't say a word. But if you pick Chandler he's gonna be whispering stupid jokes in your ear the whole time.

216
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:56,500
Oh, you are the lesser of two evils.

217
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,020
Yes!

218
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:07,240
Sven, I don't understand what you're saying. What is wrong with the flowers?

219
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,860
"Lorkins"? What the hell are "lorkins"?

220
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:10,660
I know.

221
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:18,300
Hey. Mike, if you were Swedish and you were saying the word "lorkins," what flower would that be?

222
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:20,760
Orchids? Right there!

223
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,720
That's why I'm marrying you.

224
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,300
Hello, Michael.

225
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:33,960
Joseph.

226
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,900
May I have a word with you, please?

227
00:14:49,129 --> 00:14:51,600
This is great.

228
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,940
Have a seat.

229
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:03,300
Last night l tried to welcome you into my family.

230
00:15:05,629 --> 00:15:08,879
And instead, you disrespect me.

231
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,480
I cannot allow this.

232
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,380
Are you rehearsing for some really bad Mafia movie?

233
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:18,060
More back talk.

234
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:27,500
And yes, I may be borrowing a few lines from my recent unsuccessful audition for <i>Family Honor 2:</i> <i>This A-Time It's A-Personal.</i>

235
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:33,740
Joey, I kind of have a lot to do today. What do you want?

236
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,420
I want you to take this seriously!

237
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:39,360
Phoebe is very, very important to me, okay?

238
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,880
I wanna make sure you are gonna take care of her.

239
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:45,260
Joe, I love Phoebe.

240
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,240
She's the most important thing in my life.

241
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,860
I'd die before I let anything happen to her.

242
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:55,080
That's what I wanted to hear.

243
